  triage:title "graph-orchestration/SKILL.md's Completion Invalidation step still describes the superseded merge-forward fix model, contradicting this same file's own Stack Discipline section" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr BB2-QA2-1789248000 (Final verdict FAIL, https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1444#issuecomment-5648627854, 2026-09-12T20:54:11Z; B1, req-qa ATM-QA-001, confirmed by quality-mgr via direct read), reviewed at ef7572fd0. .claude/skills/graph-orchestration/SKILL.md:427 ('Completion Invalidation,' step 4) still says: 'Dev merges forward into the next sprint's worktree, picking up any important/minor findings on the way (Step 4 in the j2 template).' This directly contradicts the Stack Discipline section 330 lines above it in the SAME file (SKILL.md:86-97: nothing below the top is ever edited; every QA finding, at every severity, goes through /triaging-findings; fixed on a new top layer) and docs/development/gh-stack-guidelines.md:54-60 (rule 5: fix work goes to the top of the stack, never a mid-stack branch). Also cites a stale 'Step 4 in the j2 template' cross-reference that no longer matches dev-fix.xml.j2's current step 4 ('Do not touch any other layer')." ;
